qBit NeoRS
===============

qBit NeoRS is a Rust/SwiftUI reimplementation of qBittorrent 5.2.4.
It is distributed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or (at your
option) any later version (see LICENSE).

It contains or is derived from the following third-party work:

* qBittorrent (https://www.qbittorrent.org), GPLv2-or-later (binary
  distribution GPLv3-or-later). Behaviour, UI texts and the WebAPI are derived
  from the qBittorrent 5.2.4 sources (pinned at reference/qBittorrent). The
  bundled WebUI (crates/qbt-core/webui/www) and the nova3 search engine helper
  scripts (crates/qbt-core/resources/nova3) are copied from qBittorrent and keep
  their original copyright headers. Copyright the qBittorrent project
  contributors; see reference/qBittorrent/AUTHORS.
  Original author: Christophe Dumez. Current maintainer: Sledgehammer999.
  Contributors: Vladimir Golovnev, Stefanos Antaris, Mohammad Dib, Mirco
  Chinelli, Ishan Arora, Arnaud Demaizière, Grigis Gaëtan, Christian Kandeler,
  Silvan Scherrer, Nick Tiskov and the contributors listed at
  https://github.com/qbittorrent/qBittorrent/graphs/contributors. The
  translations are imported from qBittorrent's, made by its volunteer
  translators (https://explore.transifex.com/sledgehammer999/qbittorrent/).
  qBittorrent carries the OpenSSL linking exception.

* rqbit / librqbit (https://github.com/ikatson/rqbit), Apache License 2.0,
  Copyright 2021 Igor Katson. The engine/ directory is a modified fork; see
  engine/LICENSE and docs/ENGINE.md for the list of changes.

* DB-IP "IP to Country Lite" database (downloaded at runtime when peer country
  resolution is enabled), Creative Commons Attribution 4.0, https://db-ip.com.

Rust crate and Swift package dependencies are listed in Cargo.lock and the
Xcode project; their licenses apply to their respective code.
